    "body": "## Purpose\n\nBalance established decode batches automatically when Model Runner V2 uses asynchronous pipeline parallelism.\n\nAsync PP makes a request eligible again after `pipeline_parallel_size` scheduler steps. Prompt-completion timing can therefore create persistent, uneven cadence groups such as Q7/Q13/Q2/Q10. This change limits established decode requests selected in each step to:\n\n```text\nceil(max_num_seqs / pipeline_parallel_size)\n```\n\nThe limit applies to both `RUNNING` requests and established decode requests resumed from `WAITING`. Prefill, chunked prefill, and chunks that complete a prompt in the current step remain uncapped because mixed batches require token-aware rather than sequence-count balancing. If priority preemption removes a selected decode, its cohort slot is restored.\n\nThe policy is active only for MRV2 `AsyncScheduler` with pipeline parallelism greater than one. PP1, synchronous scheduling, and MRV1 retain the existing effective limit of `max_num_seqs`.\n\nThis advances Workstream A of #50853.\n\n### Why this is not a duplicate\n\n#50410 is the only overlapping open PR. It caps the total number of scheduled requests, including prefill. On a matched Kimi-K3 + DSpark Mooncake replay, that global cap reduced output throughput by 8.21% versus natural scheduling. The decode-only policy here improved output throughput by 22.95% versus natural scheduling and by 33.95% versus #50410.\n\nThe distinction is implemented and tested explicitly: all 32 prompt-completing requests are scheduled together before decode is divided into two disjoint Q16 cohorts under PP2.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \\\n  .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/v1/core/test_async_scheduler.py\n\npre-commit run --files \\\n  vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py \\\n  vllm/v1/core/sched/async_scheduler.py \\\n  tests/v1/core/test_async_scheduler.py\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n- Async scheduler tests: `20 passed`\n- File-scoped pre-commit suite: passed, including Ruff, formatting, and mypy\n\nMatched Kimi-K3 + DSpark serving results on B200:\n\n| Workload | Topology | Natural cohorts | Balanced cohorts | Output tok/s change |\n|---|---|---|---|---:|\n| Fixed 64k/400, C64 | TP8/PP2 | Q19/Q13 | Q16/Q16 | +4.74% |\n| Fixed 64k/400, C64 | TP8/PP4 | Q7/Q13/Q2/Q10 | Q8/Q8/Q8/Q8 | +12.62% |\n| Mooncake trace, C64 | TP8/PP4 | natural | decode cap 8 | +22.95% |\n\nThe submitting human reviewed every changed line and the test results. AI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used to implement the reviewed change, run validation, and prepare this PR description.\n",
